1
00:00:04,619 --> 00:00:06,990
Hello, I'm Sangsoo Jeong.

2
00:00:06,991 --> 00:00:09,230
This is the last video of my class.

3
00:00:09,231 --> 00:00:11,870
Congratulations on finishing the course, everyone.

4
00:00:11,871 --> 00:00:14,670
Now that the filming is done, I feel a sense of relief.

5
00:00:14,671 --> 00:00:20,430
When I first planned this class, I was anxious about whether there was really anything I could pass on to you all.

6
00:00:20,431 --> 00:00:23,470
But as I squeezed it out, there was.

7
00:00:23,471 --> 00:00:25,310
I was surprised too.

8
00:00:25,311 --> 00:00:33,310
While filming, there were parts I was sorry I couldn't explain more concisely and systematically, and there were parts that were rewarding, like realizing, "So this is how deeply I've been thinking while I draw."

9
00:00:33,930 --> 00:00:37,020
It was hard, but it was a new experience, so it was good.

10
00:00:37,021 --> 00:00:42,540
If I ever open another class, it'll probably be a beginner class or an illustration class.

11
00:00:42,541 --> 00:00:47,100
But for now, I really want to go back to my main job and just draw.

12
00:00:47,101 --> 00:00:49,500
I'm not particularly good at speaking.

13
00:00:49,501 --> 00:00:55,420
I knew well, working as an instructor for a few months, that teaching someone isn't easy.

14
00:00:55,421 --> 00:01:02,540
I just used it in the sense of organizing the thoughts, theories, and know-how I've had while drawing, into audio and video.

15
00:01:02,710 --> 00:01:04,440
That's what I did.

16
00:01:04,441 --> 00:01:07,681
I'm not good at organizing, but once I start, I keep doing it.

17
00:01:08,199 --> 00:01:10,200
This is why getting started is important, I think.

18
00:01:10,494 --> 00:01:13,080
Thinking about it, it's the same when drawing.

19
00:01:13,081 --> 00:01:21,000
Before you start, only unorganized ideas are jumbled in your head and everything is chaotic, but once you start, before you know it, time has passed and things become concrete.

20
00:01:21,001 --> 00:01:30,801
Getting a job, publishing, a personal project, moving to the project and company I want. New starts can be scary, but don't you think a path will show itself once you take just one step?

21
00:01:31,064 --> 00:01:33,700
If you have a goal, start.

22
00:01:33,701 --> 00:01:36,500
I want to start learning 3D.

23
00:01:36,501 --> 00:01:39,780
I've been thinking about it for over five years but haven't put it into practice.

24
00:01:39,781 --> 00:01:40,781
I should try harder.

25
00:01:41,249 --> 00:01:43,220
Everyone, go learn 3D.

26
00:01:43,220 --> 00:01:55,540
When I was really into paper craft, the paper models, I once used a simple 3D program. I could only make small, simple shapes, but it helped a lot with developing my ability to grasp form.

27
00:01:55,540 --> 00:02:02,260
Even if it's not about forming shapes, people do a lot of work with buildings and various props using 3D.

28
00:02:02,261 --> 00:02:07,060
When I was a beginner, drawing weapons at an angle was hard, so I got help from 3D.

29
00:02:07,061 --> 00:02:08,061
Like this.

30
00:02:09,954 --> 00:02:13,511
Actually, when you're studying, even if it's hard, drawing it yourself is better.

31
00:02:13,950 --> 00:02:21,310
But if you already know how to draw to a certain degree and want to improve further, learning 3D seems like a good choice.

32
00:02:23,190 --> 00:02:24,440
Let me get back on topic.

33
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:29,240
I think all of you have goals and plans for the future.

34
00:02:29,241 --> 00:02:34,840
To those preparing for jobs and those who are professionals, I support your future path and new challenges.

35
00:02:34,841 --> 00:02:36,360
I'll say goodbye here.

36
00:02:36,361 --> 00:02:37,361
Goodbye, everyone.
